A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

## The rule

A report is a duplicate only when it shares a **demonstrated cause** with an open ticket
([decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause), replacing the preserved decision 0001):

1. Look up the tenant's locale and booking form, and check the report channel and body.
2. Compare causes with `causeOf` and `sameCause` in `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`, then check the reproduction.
3. Merge only into the matching cause's ticket. Count each report ID once, even in overlapping exports.
4. For #4471, route the day-first booking-v3 form path to the hint issue; other supported day-first paths go to parser.
5. Keep missing-tenant, unknown-cause and conflicting evidence separate for investigation.

<Callout>
Subjects and intake tags are search clues, not merge criteria. Matching subjects may have
different causes; different subjects may have the same cause. See the reviewed incident page.
</Callout>

[Reviewed #4471 and its separate issues](/kb/incidents/4471-review).

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Do not merge yet. Reproduce the failing path, confirm the tenant and channel, and ask for
missing evidence. Preserve one-day descriptions for investigation; do not assume a timezone cause.
Rebuild the views with new exports so the desk keeps routing new reports correctly.
